description:
To print this template from a Print Format, write <code>{{ render_web_template("Template Name", input_name=value, ...) }}</code> there. Each input is a row in the Fields table above: its fieldname is the name to pass, and its type and Required say what to pass. For example <code>{{ render_web_template("Student Statement", student=doc.name) }}</code>. Context Prep turns the inputs into what the template reads; <b>Test PDF</b> in the toolbar asks for them and prints the result.<br><br>Frappe places the letter head chosen in the print dialog only on its standard format, so a Print Format that should carry one includes the same markup around the call:<pre style="margin-top: 6px; white-space: pre-wrap"><code>{% if letter_head and not no_letterhead %}
&lt;div {% if print_settings.repeat_header_footer %}id=&quot;header-html&quot; class=&quot;hidden-pdf&quot;{% endif %}&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;letter-head&quot;&gt;{{ letter_head }}&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
{% endif %}

{{ render_web_template(&quot;Student Statement&quot;, student=doc.name) }}

{% if footer and not no_letterhead %}
&lt;div {% if print_settings.repeat_header_footer %}id=&quot;footer-html&quot; class=&quot;visible-pdf&quot;{% endif %}&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;letter-head-footer&quot;&gt;{{ footer }}&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
{% endif %}</code></pre>
